<title>
Auto Steering Lock Inspection
</title>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Remove steering column lower cover and steering column hole cover.
</ptxt>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Steering column lower cover: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206001"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Steering column hole cover: 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A9306002"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</s1>
<s1>
<ptxt>
Measure voltage between terminals “1” – “5” and ground respectively under conditions described in the table below. If check result is not as specified, check auto steering lock wire harness for open or short and if auto steering lock wire harness is in good condition, replace auto steering lock (1). 
<intxreftitleoff1 refid = "AENLSB0A6206013"><img src = "..\icon\intxreftitleoff.gif"/></intxreftitleoff1>
</ptxt>
<attention3>
<ptxt>
*: Voltage can be checked only for a short time while locking or releasing auto steering lock.
</ptxt>
</attention3>
